@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "For Staff";
}

<section>
    <h1>Kasper College Staff Portal & Faculty Information</h1>
    <p>Official Guidance, Academic Administration, IT Services, HR Policies, and Campus Facilities for Staff</p>

    <div class = "textBox">
        <h2>1. News & College Announcements</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Software Engineering Student of the Year Awards: </b>Kasper College recently hosted the annual National Software Engineering Student of the Year Awards in the Main Lecture Theatre. Shortlisted candidates from 24 institutions nationwide attended the one-day symposium and showcase.</li>
            <li><b>£1.2M High-Performance Computing Grant: </b>The Department of Computing & Digital Technologies has been awarded £1.2 million from the Engineering and Physical Sciences Research Council (EPSRC) to install a cutting-edge GPU cluster dedicated to AI ethics and edge-computing research.</li>
            <li><b>National Teaching Fellowships: </b>Congratulations to Dr. Sarah Jenkins (Senior Lecturer in Cyber Security) and Prof. David Chen (Reader in Interactive Media) on being awarded National Teaching Fellowships for pedagogical innovation.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class = "textBox">
        <h2>2. Academic Registry & Quality Assurance</h2>
        <p>The Academic Registry oversees academic regulations, assessment standards, student records, module evaluation, and course validation.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Assessment & Moderation: </b>All summative assessment briefs must undergo internal peer moderation 4 weeks prior to release. Sample scripts (10% or minimum 6 scripts) must be submitted for external examiner scrutiny.</li>
            <li><b>Grade Submission Deadlines: </b>Autumn semester module results must be finalized on the Student Records System (SRS) by 17:00 on Friday, 22 January 2027.</li>
            <li><b>Extenuating Circumstances & Academic Appeals: </b>Faculty panels review claims weekly. Staff should direct distressed students to the Student Support Desk for initial evidence validation.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class = "textBox">
        <h2>3. Human Resources, Payroll & Staff Wellbeing</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>HR Service Portal: </b>Staff can access monthly payslips, P60s, annual leave booking (35 days plus bank holidays), and sickness reporting via the internal PeopleHR portal.</li>
            <li><b>Employee Assistance Programme (EAP): </b>Free 24/7 confidential counseling, financial advice, and mental health support available to all permanent and fixed-term staff via HealthAssured (Freephone: 0800 030 5182).</li>
            <li><b>Staff Development Fund: </b>Full-time faculty are eligible for up to £1,500 annually toward conference attendance, professional certifications (e.g., AWS, Cisco, Adobe), and academic journal publication fees.</li>
            <li><b>Cycle-to-Work & EV Salary Sacrifice: </b>Tax-free bicycle purchases and electric vehicle leasing schemes available through the HR Benefits hub.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class = "textBox">
        <h2>4. IT Services & Classroom Technology Support</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Single Sign-On (SSO) & MFA: </b>All staff accounts require Microsoft Authenticator multi-factor authentication for logging into campus systems and remote VPN access.</li>
            <li><b>Moodle VLE & Panopto Lecture Capture: </b>All lecture theatres and seminar rooms feature automated recording. Course materials and reading lists must be populated 2 weeks before teaching commences.</li>
            <li><b>Classroom AV Hotline: </b>Immediate in-class technical assistance is available by dialing extension 2222 from any lectern telephone.</li>
            <li><b>Software Licenses: </b>Staff may request specialized software installations for teaching labs by submitting an IT Helpdesk ticket at least 15 working days prior to term start.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class = "textBox">
        <h2>5. Room, Laboratory & Event Bookings</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Timetabled Teaching Rooms: </b>Managed centrally by the Academic Timetabling Team. Ad-hoc bookings for extra tutorials or student workshops can be made via the Resource Scheduler system.</li>
            <li><b>Specialist Computing Labs: </b>SOC labs, VR suites, and maker workshops require certified technician supervision when booked outside standard timetable hours.</li>
            <li><b>Conference & Meeting Rooms: </b>The Boardroom (Room 302) and Executive Suite (Room 305) can be reserved via Outlook calendar invites.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class = "textBox">
        <h2>6. Health, Safety, First Aid & Emergency Evacuation</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Emergency Numbers: </b>Campus Security & First Aid Emergency: dial 3333 (Internal) or (01321) 2340 333.</li>
            <li><b>Fire Alarm Testing: </b>Conducted every Tuesday at 08:45. In the event of a continuous alarm, evacuate immediately via the nearest fire exit to Assembly Point A (Main Campus Plaza) or Point B (West Car Park).</li>
            <li><b>Display Screen Equipment (DSE): </b>All staff must complete an annual DSE self-assessment to ensure ergonomic workstation setup.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class = "textBox">
        <h2>7. Catering & Hospitality Bookings</h2>
        <p>Contact Catering Services (catering@kaspercollege.ac.uk) for internal hospitality, working lunches, guest speaker refreshments, and departmental celebrations. Minimum 48 hours notice required.</p>
    </div>

    <div class = "table">

    </div>

</section>